From 8fd9bcf48bef6eb6dd361b86a3e6fb79ad98e702 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: François Guerraz <kubrick@fgv6.net>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: flowtable: use the route device for neighbour xmit

Since 6.18.45, which backported commit b5964aac51e0 ("netfilter: flowtable:
consolidate xmit path") and commit 2bdc536c9da7 ("netfilter: always set
route tuple out ifindex"), FLOW_OFFLOAD_XMIT_NEIGH flows are transmitted on
the device whose index is stored in the tuple instead of the route device.

When the flowtable lists a bridge but not its ports, forward path
discovery towards a host behind a plain Ethernet or DSA bridge port
records the port the FDB points to as the output device.
nft_dev_forward_path() stores its ifindex before it checks whether the
discovered ingress device is part of the flowtable. That check fails, so
the flow remains a neighbour flow, but it is now transmitted directly on
that port:

- The flow does not follow FDB changes. Packets in either direction
  refresh it, so when the host moves to another port of the bridge (a
  bond failover, a moved cable, or from Ethernet to Wi-Fi for a flow set
  up while the host was on Ethernet), the router keeps sending to the old
  port and the connection stalls.
- Transmission skips the bridge device's qdisc, the bridge output and
  postrouting hooks, and bridge VLAN egress processing. With taggers such
  as vsc73xx-8021q, frames without the bridge forwarding mark also get
  the port's standalone VLAN, which the switch drops once bridge join has
  removed it.

Before 6.18.45 neighbour flows were transmitted on the route device, the
bridge, which picks the port for each packet. Do that again. The
neighbour lookup already uses the route device, and nothing else reads
the output ifindex of a neighbour flow. The NULL check of the looked-up
device goes away with the lookup: the device of a cached route is never
NULL (dst_dev_put() replaces it with blackhole_netdev), and the
neighbour lookup that follows already uses it unchecked. Direct xmit
flows are unchanged. VLAN and PPPoE uppers were already recorded as the
output device, so flows through them keep their output device.

This also covers the failed path discovery case handled by OpenWrt patch
699: neighbour transmission no longer uses its fallback output ifindex.

Mainline with commit 871df5007eda ("netfilter: flowtable: bail out if
forward path cannot be discovered") does not offload a flow when
discovery fails or the discovered device is not in the flowtable, which
avoids this case. That commit is not in 6.18.55 and does not apply to its
older path discovery code.

Tested with 6.18.55 and 699 in a QEMU VM, with a routed TCP download to a
host that has an active-backup bond over two ports of a bridge, the
bridge and the server side interface in a software flowtable, and a
failover after about 4.5 s. Without this change, IPv4 and IPv6 downloads
reported 0 bit/s for the rest of the 14 s run. With it, both continued
without a visible interruption. In both kernels the forward chain
counter stayed at 10 packets for transfers of tens of gigabytes. The
bridge output counter stayed at 14-18 packets without the change and
grew with the transfer with it. Also in use on a GL.iNet GL-BE9300
(qualcommbe).

Fixes: b5964aac51e0 ("netfilter: flowtable: consolidate xmit path")
Fixes: 2bdc536c9da7 ("netfilter: always set route tuple out ifindex")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: François Guerraz <kubrick@fgv6.net>
---
 net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_ip.c | 12 ++----------
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

--- a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_ip.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_ip.c
@@ -463,11 +463,7 @@ nf_flow_offload_ip_hook(void *priv, stru
 	switch (tuplehash->tuple.xmit_type) {
 	case FLOW_OFFLOAD_XMIT_NEIGH:
 		rt = dst_rtable(tuplehash->tuple.dst_cache);
-		xmit.outdev = dev_get_by_index_rcu(state->net, tuplehash->tuple.ifidx);
-		if (!xmit.outdev) {
-			flow_offload_teardown(flow);
-			return NF_DROP;
-		}
+		xmit.outdev = rt->dst.dev;
 		neigh = ip_neigh_gw4(rt->dst.dev, rt_nexthop(rt, flow->tuplehash[!dir].tuple.src_v4.s_addr));
 		if (IS_ERR(neigh)) {
 			flow_offload_teardown(flow);
@@ -768,11 +764,7 @@ nf_flow_offload_ipv6_hook(void *priv, st
 	switch (tuplehash->tuple.xmit_type) {
 	case FLOW_OFFLOAD_XMIT_NEIGH:
 		rt = dst_rt6_info(tuplehash->tuple.dst_cache);
-		xmit.outdev = dev_get_by_index_rcu(state->net, tuplehash->tuple.ifidx);
-		if (!xmit.outdev) {
-			flow_offload_teardown(flow);
-			return NF_DROP;
-		}
+		xmit.outdev = rt->dst.dev;
 		neigh = ip_neigh_gw6(rt->dst.dev, rt6_nexthop(rt, &flow->tuplehash[!dir].tuple.src_v6));
 		if (IS_ERR(neigh)) {
 			flow_offload_teardown(flow);
